00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.060
I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:35.580
Always do your own research before putting real money to work. Canadian TFSA holders,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:42.360
eyeing energy exposure should note oils pre-market lift as US futures point to mixed open ahead of

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:54.360
big tech earnings. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,509, up 0.9%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 25,800

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:06.380
137, up 1.3%. The TSX composite closed at 35,369, up 1.2%. Sentiment remains pinned on corporate

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:13.160
earnings with more S&amp;P 500 companies raising outlooks than cutting them. The Bank of Canada is

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:18.920
holding rates steady, absent major escalation on Iran while the European Central Bank decision

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:24.800
arrives Thursday. Energy leads intraday moves as oil rises ahead of the earnings wave.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:32.000
About 21 days ago, the show selected GIS on an earning surprise entry. That position closed with

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:39.580
a gain of 3.76%. The result illustrates how revenue beats can still deliver when sector rotation

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:44.600
aligns with the move. Revenue strength alone proved sufficient in that instance.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:51.260
The outcome serves as a reminder that timing with broader flows matters. Our simulated portfolio

00:01:51.260 --> 00:02:01.220
sits at a cumulative profit of $266.87 across 42 trades. The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:07.840
stands at positive 6.6%. Earnings breakout positioning targets companies raising forward

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.340
guidance instead of just clearing the current quarter. The current environment favors names with

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:20.980
sustained demand visibility into the second half, given the number of S&amp;P 500 firms lifting outlooks.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:27.060
Screen using consensus revision data on Bloomberg terminal or free alternatives like Yahoo Finance

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:33.640
earnings calendars. Then cross check against 20 day average volume to confirm institutional follow

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:39.580
through. This approach has worked best in the early to mid stages of earnings season when macro

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:46.120
volatility stays moderate. The main risk is a sudden rotation out of growth into defensives if

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:53.600
tariff headlines escalate. Size every position at 1-2% of the portfolio to limit single name drawdown.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:59.800
Now we turn to today's practice investment update. This is a simulated trade for educational

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:06.140
purposes only. No new position opened today. Oil price strength ahead of big tech earnings

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:12.020
creates potential sector rotation into energy. We are watching for energy names to hold above the

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:19.060
50-day moving average with volume above the 20-day average. Current pre-market action lacks that volume

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:26.520
confirmation. Geopolitical headlines could reverse oil gains quickly. No entry occurs until the volume

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:35.960
spike materializes. This pause shows how to define explicit trigger criteria rather than chasing

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:42.720
the exact data point required before committing capital. Yesterday's trade review finds no newly closed

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:48.940
trade since the last review. The most recent practice investment remains open and pending scheduled

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:56.420
evaluation. No new realized result appears today. The Nielsen IQ analytics platform expands its

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:02.440
circle K agreement to deliver granular merchandising and pricing data across 12 or more countries.

