00:04:51.560 --> 00:05:00.540
Avanté reported fiscal 2026 results. Revenue reached $37.2 million. That total marks a 10.3%

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:10.940
year-over-year increase. Adjusted EBDA arrived at $2.3 million. The EBDA figure reflects 30% growth.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:19.040
Expansion in the NSSG segment drove the improvement. Recurring revenue rose 24% over the same period.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:26.560
Listeners can add Avanté to a TFSA watch list for any pullback below recent support after the print.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:34.680
Natural G lifted its full-year 2026 outlook. The utility acted after posting robust first half results.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:41.040
Guidance revision followed strong performance across the first six months. Investors should review

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:47.720
natural G exposure in global energy ETFs. The move positions the name ahead of the next earnings

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:53.000
window. The outlook increase reflects sustained operational strength through the half.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:06:01.180
BTIG initiated coverage on keel infrastructure with a buy rating. Analysts pointed to power asset

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:07.620
strength as the primary driver. The new coverage highlights the value of those assets. Investors

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:14.580
can screen utility sector ETFs for any rebalancing flows. Names with similar asset profiles may attract

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:21.260
comparable attention. The initiation adds visibility to the infrastructure space. Foundry is pulling

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:28.360
Bitcoin miners on a BIP 110 proposal. The measure aims to reduce transaction data size. The

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:34.320
mining pool is gathering customer input on the change. Crypto participants should cross-check any

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:40.540
allocation against two independent price feeds. The step precedes any potential position adjustments.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:48.180
Verification helps confirm data integrity before acting. Our simulated portfolio across 42 trades

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:58.340
shows a 55% win rate with 23 wins, 18 losses and one break even. Cumulative profit stands at $266.87.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:06.420
The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ is positive 6.6% across 37 benchmark trades.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:15.660
Average return per trade sits at 0.64%. The current streak is two losses. Our AI analysis continues

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:21.520
learning from recent patterns and adjusting screens accordingly. Imagine you bought a covered call

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:30.040
ETF last week when energy names lifted on oil strength. Your limit order filled at $42.18. Between

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:36.560
the click and the fill, the bid asks spread on that ETF widened from 3 cents to 14 cents in the first

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:43.220
25 minutes of the session. The mechanism at work is time value decay combined with liquidity withdrawal.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:50.780
The call you sold collected an 85 cent premium, but 60% of that premium is theta eroding daily

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:58.680
once the stock stops moving. The Greeks update in real time. Delta on that call moved from 0.35 to

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:05.520
0.42 as the underlying ticked higher, changing your effective hedge ratio without any action on your

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:11.700
part. Professionals always check open interest and the 20 day average volume on the option chain

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:17.420
before placing the order. The biggest mistake with options is treating the quoted premium as

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:22.820
guaranteed income without accounting for early assignment risk on dividends. Instead,

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:29.500
always model the position at 3 volatility levels before entry. Before we wrap, open your brokerage

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:35.460
screener tomorrow and filter for energy names with year-to-date revenue growth above 10% and 20

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:41.640
day average volume above 500,000 shares. That's it for today's modern investing techniques.

